CORE
main.cpp
--cpp11 --unwind 5 --no-unwinding-assertions
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
main exercises std::set::insert, std::set::size and std::set::count.  The
libstdc++ red-black-tree insertion (std::_Rb_tree_insert_and_rebalance) is
defined in the compiled library, not the headers, so CBMC provides a model
for it (cpp_typecheck_stdlib.cpp) that performs the binary-search-tree link
and header (root/leftmost/rightmost) maintenance -- sufficient for the
ordered-container find/count/size semantics.
